      "message": "feat(ui): edit each milling tool kind by its parameters inside the outline editor\n\nThe Draw cutter view now carries the numbers each milling kind's outline\nis drawn from (cutter Ø, the kind's tip - ball R, corner R, point or cone\nangle - flute length, shank Ø and length) plus a neck, editing the same\ndraft as the editor's fields. A Parametric outline is redrawn from them;\na Custom one is carried onto the new numbers (cutter_fit::refit: tip\nregenerated from the kind, the drawing above the flutes kept and moved,\nclamped to the shank), so outline and numbers keep agreeing.\n\nReshapeTool lands the numbers and the drawn cutter together, one undo\nstep, judged against the new numbers; Apply cutter and the editor's\nApply use it instead of refusing a number edit under a drawn cutter.\nMCP: set_tool_cutter_params; get_tool_cutter_profile reports the neck.\n\nRefs #93\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
